# Citation metadata for iscc (https://citation-file-format.github.io/).
#
# Pending, to be filled in when they exist (no placeholder values are given for them):
#   - version and date-released: set when release v0.4.0 is made;
#   - doi: assigned when release v0.4.0 is archived;
#   - preferred-citation: the preprint that describes iscc, which is in preparation.
# The author list follows the author block of the preprint. That block is still empty in the
# manuscript, so only the author of the software (LICENSE, pyproject.toml) is listed here for now.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use iscc, please cite it as below, together with the preprint that describes it once it is available."
title: "iscc: in silico cancer center"
abstract: >-
  iscc (in silico cancer center) is a Python package that grows a tumor under copy-number and
  driver selection in a field of glands, stroma and an optional metastatic site, where selection
  depends on the niche, and carries the same cells through biopsy and dissociation into bulk and
  single-cell DNA, RNA and spatial transcriptomics data, down to sequencing reads, while keeping
  the ground truth of every cell, clone and niche.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ferreira
    given-names: Pedro F.
repository-code: "https://github.com/pedrofale/iscc"
url: "https://pedrofale.github.io/iscc/"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - tumor evolution
  - simulation
  - single-cell sequencing
  - spatial transcriptomics
  - benchmarking
